# This is a Linux/POSIX project that may be edited from Windows, where
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise rewrite checkouts to CRLF. That breaks
# real things on the target platform: /bin/sh rejects a script whose lines end
# in \r, and Make mis-reads recipe lines. Pin everything to LF in the
# repository and in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish artefacts that must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.gz  binary
*.zip binary
